<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cerball mac Dúnlainge</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 888</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Carroll, King of Osraige</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cerball mac Dúnlainge was king of Osraige in Ireland from about 842 until his death in 888. By fighting and allying with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Viking</a> leaders, and by exploiting rivalries between the kings of Munster and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ui-neill">Uí Néill</a>, he made his small kingdom a major power. Icelandic sagas remember him as Kjarval, an ancestor of many Icelandic settler families.</p></div>
